/******************************************************************************
* djinterp [re_std]                                                      cstdlib
*
* <cstdlib> umbrella header:
*   Aggregates the granular headers under /inc/djinterp/re_std/cstdlib/.
* Mirrors the standard <cstdlib> convenience header and adds no symbols of
* its own.
*
*   THE WHOLE MODULE IS RE-EXPORTS, AND THAT IS THE CORRECT DESIGN:
*   Every function here is a contract with the C runtime rather than a
* piece of library logic. malloc's blocks must return to the runtime's
* free; atexit's handlers must land on the runtime's list; getenv reads
* the process environment; the multibyte functions read the active
* locale. A reimplementation would be a second, disconnected copy of
* state the process already has one of -- so re_std::malloc IS
* std::malloc, and a pointer crosses between the two spellings freely.
*
*   This is the same reasoning as <new> and <typeinfo>, and the opposite
* of <bitset> or <expected>, which are pure library code re_std owns
* outright.
*
*   GRANULARITY IS BY FAMILY, NOT BY SYMBOL -- A DOCUMENTED EXCEPTION:
*   The module's forty-odd symbols are grouped into eight headers by what
* they do. The usual one-symbol-per-header rule exists to narrow
* compile-time dependencies, and it has nothing to narrow here: every
* symbol has the identical dependency, <cstdlib> itself. Forty headers
* each holding one using-declaration and the same #include would buy
* nothing. Families are the useful unit instead -- a caller who wants
* only the termination functions includes process_control.hpp:
*
*     string_conversion.hpp   atof, atoi, atol, atoll, strtod, strtof,
*                             strtold, strtol, strtoll, strtoul, strtoull
*     random.hpp              rand, srand
*     memory.hpp              malloc, calloc, realloc, free,
*                             aligned_alloc (gated)
*     process_control.hpp     abort, exit, _Exit, atexit,
*                             quick_exit / at_quick_exit (gated)
*     environment.hpp         getenv, system
*     search_sort.hpp         qsort, bsearch
*     integer_arithmetic.hpp  abs, labs, llabs, div, ldiv, lldiv,
*                             div_t, ldiv_t, lldiv_t
*     multibyte.hpp           mblen, mbtowc, wctomb, mbstowcs, wcstombs
*
*   THE MACROS HAVE NO re_std:: SPELLING:
*   EXIT_SUCCESS, EXIT_FAILURE, RAND_MAX, MB_CUR_MAX and NULL are macros
* and are therefore surfaced exactly as the standard header supplies
* them.
*
*   TWO SYMBOLS ARE CONDITIONAL. Both are gated on a D_RE_STD_HAS_*
* macro, and where the runtime lacks them the name is absent rather than
* redirected to a near-equivalent with different semantics:
*
*     D_RE_STD_HAS_ALIGNED_ALLOC   0 on MSVC and pre-10.15 Apple
*     D_RE_STD_HAS_QUICK_EXIT      0 on Apple
*
*   WHERE re_std HAS A BETTER ANSWER, THE FAMILY HEADER SAYS SO:
*   re_std::sort over qsort, <random> over rand, ::operator new over
* malloc, from_chars over atoi. The C functions are surfaced for
* interoperation and for porting, not as recommendations.
*
*
* path:      /inc/djinterp/re_std/cstdlib/cstdlib
* link(s):   TBA
* author(s): TBA                                           created: 2026.08.25
******************************************************************************/

